#: {{ux|en|The doctor’s bedside manner was especially '''winsome'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|author=Jonathan Freke Slingsby [pseudonym; {{w|John Francis Waller}}]|title=Slingsby in Scotland. Part II.—Conclusion.|magazine=[[w:Dublin University Magazine|The Dublin University Magazine, a Literary and Political Journal]]|location=Dublin|publisher=[[w:Gill (publisher)|James McGlashan]], 50 [[w:O'Connell Street|Upper Sackville-St.]]; London: W[illia]m S[omerville] Orr|month=October|year=1851|volume=XXXVIII|number=CCXXVI|section=stanza I|page=494|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=rJk6AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA494|oclc=841086102|passage=Will ye keep your troth to me, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay? / Will ye keep your troth to me, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay? / Will ye keep your troth to me? / My ain true luve will ye be? / Then meet me at the trysting tree, / '''Winsome''' Annie Ramsay.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=Episode 13, Nausicaa|page=333|passage=Gerty MacDowell who was seated near her companions, lost in thought, gazing far away into the distance was in very truth as fair a specimen of '''winsome''' Irish girlhood as one could wish to see.}}
#* {{RQ:Song Chinese in Singapore|chapter=XI|page=377|format=full|passage=He [Ching Keng Lee] is a man of fine physique and above the height of the average Straits-born, with a shrewd business head, and affable and '''winsome''' manners, and continues to take a keen interest in public affairs.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|author=David Alexander|chapter=When the Rain Stops|title=Hangman’s Dozen|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Roy Publishers|year=1961|page=216|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=klZRAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA216|oclc=1118558|passage=The pink wallpaper of the nursery was decorated with a Noah's Ark of friendly lions and comical giraffes and '''winsome''' elephants.}}

